[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/267276070","html_url":"https://github.com/netty/netty/issues/6134#issuecomment-267276070","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/6134","id":267276070,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2NzI3NjA3MA==","user":{"login":"normanmaurer","id":439362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/439362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer","html_url":"https://github.com/normanmaurer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-12-15T09:13:16Z","updated_at":"2016-12-15T09:13:16Z","body":"Sounds good... you want to do a PR?\n\n> Am 15.12.2016 um 08:51 schrieb Jo Kin <notifications@github.com>:\n> \n> Running Netty on a Java-VM on IBM z/OS leads to unnecessary warnings.\n> \n> You have to know that Unix System Services of IBM z/OS offers PIDs greater than 2^22, as assumed in DefaultChannelID (see Issue 2706)\n> \n> Welcome to Unix System Services ZOSU of\n> z / O S Version 2 Release 2\n> $ ps\n> PID TTY TIME CMD\n> 41 ttyp0000 0:00 /bin/sh\n> 50332311 ttyp0000 0:00 /bin/ps <== !\n> $\n> \n> Expected behavior\n> \n> Netty should accept valid PIDs coming from any OS. It is a little bit infelicitous to assume that the Linux64 limits are valid for all OS which supports JAVA.\n> \n> Actual behavior\n> \n> Even DefaultChannelID's auto-mechanism succeeded in detecting the correct PID on z/OS the PID is discarded by later check and replaced by a random value.\n> \n> Dec 15, 2016 6:05:49 AM io.netty.channel.DefaultChannelId defaultProcessId WARNING: Failed to find the current process ID from '50332208'; using a random value: 474712\n> \n> Steps to reproduce\n> \n> Start any Netty-using application (i.e. your sample io.netty.example.echo.EchoServer) on IBM Mainframe z/OS. With a little luck the arising PID violates the limit in Netty.\n> \n> Minimal yet complete reproducer code (or URL to code)\n> \n> io.netty.example.echo.EchoServer\n> \n> Netty version\n> \n> 4.1.5\n> \n> JVM version (e.g. java -version)\n> \n> java version \"1.7.0\"\n> Java(TM) SE Runtime Environment (build pmz3170_27sr3fp40-20160422_01(SR3 FP40))\n> IBM J9 VM (build 2.7, JRE 1.7.0 z/OS s390-31 20160406_298393 (JIT enabled, AOT enabled)\n> J9VM - R27_Java727_SR3_20160406_0942_B298393\n> JIT - tr.r13.java_20160328_114186\n> GC - R27_Java727_SR3_20160406_0942_B298393\n> J9CL - 20160406_298393)\n> JCL - 20160421_01 based on Oracle jdk7u101-b14\n> \n> OS version (e.g. uname -a)\n> \n> IBM z/OS 2.2\n> $ uname -a\n> OS/390 ZOSU 25.00 04 2828\n> \n> —\n> You are receiving this because you are subscribed to this thread.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub, or mute the thread.\n> \n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/comments/267276070/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"normanmaurer","id":439362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/439362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer","html_url":"https://github.com/normanmaurer","followers_url":"